;; ---- wire 20 :process/spawn: a helper forked before the sandbox ----
;; The removed loader ran programs from its unsandboxed supervisor. This
;; runtime has no supervisor, and a child of the sandboxed process would
;; inherit its seccomp filter and its 64 MiB address-space limit. So when
;; wire 20 is granted, kxrt-start forks one helper before the limits and the
;; filter. The helper keeps its own copy of the grant and decides every
;; request itself (tools/linux_static_handlers.kotoba ops 33..42), then forks
;; and executes the program, writing the request's stdin payload (after
;; STDIN_SEP) to the child's stdin, then closing it; the sandboxed guest only frames a request on one
;; pipe and reads one answer on another (a u32 little-endian length, then a
;; kind byte and the bytes: A an answer, R a refusal index, M a malformed
;; request). The helper runs no guest code and ends at end of file.
;; Grant: KEXE_CAP_RESOURCES_20 (programs, colon-separated canonical absolute
;; paths, 1..16 distinct), KEXE_SPAWN_ENV (names, colon-separated, 0..16),
;; KEXE_SPAWN_PATH_LOOKUP (1, or 0 / absent). A malformed grant exits 2; an
;; absent or empty program list grants nothing.
;; State at G+2048: 2048 program map (16 x 4096), 2056 name map (16 x 256),
;; 2064 programs, 2072 names, 2080 lookup, 2088 the request fd and 2096 the
;; answer fd (guest side), 2104 the helper's pid, 2112.. program lengths,
;; 2240.. name lengths.
;; Helper buffers in the io buffer: +1 MiB request, +2 MiB argv strings,
;; +2 MiB+4096 argv, +2 MiB+8192 envp, +3 MiB output, +4 MiB status and
;; times, +5 MiB the answer frame.
(defn- kxrt-le32 [b :i64] :i64
